{
  "$comment": "The mutation workflow's shard jobs (stryker/base.mjs, TP_MUTATION_SHARD; docs/adr/0066, Part 4). Every file a package's config mutates is in exactly one shard, and a shard runs its files in full. The split balances the wall time and summed mutant time Stryker 10.1.1 measured at 49514e8 (the mutation scout's 10.1.1 reports, 4 shared CPUs): money (34 s) with ledger (2 min 28 s); packets' scan.ts (939 s of mutant time) against the rest of packets (997 s), and the calculation words (packages/packets/src/explain*, docs/adr/0072) in a shard of their own, so packets-rest keeps its time; pricing's engine.ts (1,232 s), recompute.ts (952 s) and the rest of pricing (804 s). noMutants lists the files a shard holds that Stryker 10.1.1 finds no mutant in (imports, re-exports, types and `as const` values, which its instrumenter reads as types; tools/stryker/shards.test.ts holds each to that), the only files a shard's report may leave out: the gate requires every other file of the shard in it.",
